WEBVTT

1
00:00:05.645 --> 00:00:07.644
<i>In Toronto's war
on crime.</i>

2
00:00:07.645 --> 00:00:10.161
<i>the worst offenders
are pursued by the detectives</i>

3
00:00:10.162 --> 00:00:13.057
<i>of the Specialized Criminal
Investigations Unit.</i>

4
00:00:13.058 --> 00:00:14.678
<i>These are their stories.</i>

5
00:00:38.093 --> 00:00:40.851
Barbara. you should've
brought flowers

6
00:00:40.852 --> 00:00:42.333
for her birthday.

7
00:00:42.334 --> 00:00:44.575
I don't need flowers.

8
00:00:44.576 --> 00:00:47.402
I need news.
Detective Michaels.

9
00:00:47.403 --> 00:00:48.989
I can't go on like this.

10
00:00:48.990 --> 00:00:50.886
We've run out of leads.

11
00:00:54.024 --> 00:00:55.645
Find new ones.

12
00:01:01.852 --> 00:01:03.989
Let's go.

13
00:01:03.990 --> 00:01:05.540
Looking good. Ainsley.

14
00:01:05.541 --> 00:01:06.885
Alright.

15
00:01:06.886 --> 00:01:08.610
Love that pose.

16
00:01:11.817 --> 00:01:13.092
Alright. I think we're done.

17
00:01:17.921 --> 00:01:19.368
Stay for a drink?

18
00:01:19.369 --> 00:01:21.955
Thanks. Riley.
but I think I'm just gonna go.

19
00:01:23.610 --> 00:01:25.057
Everything okay?

20
00:01:25.058 --> 00:01:26.403
Sure.

21
00:01:28.541 --> 00:01:30.541
Never gonna be hotter
than I am now. right?

22
00:01:35.748 --> 00:01:43.885
<i>♪ Gonna be the last
girls at the party ♪</i>

23
00:01:43.886 --> 00:01:45.575
<i>♪ Gonna be the last girls</i>

24
00:01:45.576 --> 00:01:48.402
<i>♪ I might need a smoke break</i>

25
00:01:48.403 --> 00:01:50.506
<i>♪ 'Cause you miss out on
the shots that you don't take ♪</i>

26
00:01:50.507 --> 00:01:52.644
Stunning.

27
00:01:52.645 --> 00:01:54.954
The clothes
or the ladies. Craig?

28
00:01:54.955 --> 00:01:57.990
Wendy. there's only one
lady in this room for me.

29
00:01:59.024 --> 00:02:01.333
<i>♪ Everyone's gone home</i>

30
00:02:01.334 --> 00:02:04.092
No open drinks
near the samples!

31
00:02:04.093 --> 00:02:06.023
Hey. Ainsley. is that your name?

32
00:02:06.024 --> 00:02:08.299
The girls have to get ready
for the finale. Help them.

33
00:02:08.300 --> 00:02:10.333
Be helpful.

34
00:02:10.334 --> 00:02:11.678
Hold this.

35
00:02:11.679 --> 00:02:12.920
Are you even
in the right look?!

36
00:02:12.921 --> 00:02:14.333
It's the last flavor.

37
00:02:16.679 --> 00:02:19.713
Tanya. this is not
what I expected!

38
00:02:19.714 --> 00:02:22.989
Hey. ladies?
Eyes on me. please.

39
00:02:22.990 --> 00:02:26.437
Remember what we talked about.
Powerful and fluid.

40
00:02:26.438 --> 00:02:28.333
Let's have some fun.

41
00:02:28.334 --> 00:02:30.264
Mr. Sharpe.

42
00:02:30.265 --> 00:02:32.127
Excuse me.

43
00:02:37.265 --> 00:02:40.126
<i>♪ It's only three. right?
It's only four. right? ♪</i>

44
00:02:40.127 --> 00:02:42.644
<i>♪ It's only five. right?
It's only six. right? ♪</i>

45
00:02:45.058 --> 00:02:48.816
<i>♪ Gonna be the last
girls at the party ♪</i>

46
00:02:48.817 --> 00:02:51.230
<i>♪ No hard feelings</i>

47
00:02:51.231 --> 00:02:54.609
<i>♪ We're not leaving</i>

48
00:02:54.610 --> 00:02:57.092
<i>♪ While you're sleeping ♪</i>

49
00:02:57.093 --> 00:02:59.609
You wish you were out there?

50
00:02:59.610 --> 00:03:02.644
No. I appreciate this job.

51
00:03:02.645 --> 00:03:05.402
But. yeah.

52
00:03:05.403 --> 00:03:07.954
Well. we'll
have lunch on Monday

53
00:03:07.955 --> 00:03:11.540
and we'll talk
about your future.

54
00:03:11.541 --> 00:03:14.023
You can still get me
into the after-party. right?

55
00:03:14.024 --> 00:03:15.333
Oh. my God.

56
00:03:21.748 --> 00:03:24.609
I'm leaving
and you should too.

57
00:03:24.610 --> 00:03:26.437
It's about to become
hunting hour.

58
00:03:26.438 --> 00:03:28.402
The plus one remains.

59
00:03:30.817 --> 00:03:32.920
Oh. uh. sorry.

60
00:03:32.921 --> 00:03:34.437
It's okay.
Let me get you another.

61
00:03:34.438 --> 00:03:37.368
- Are you a designer?
- Cosmetic surgeon.

62
00:03:37.369 --> 00:03:38.851
Mm.

63
00:03:38.852 --> 00:03:40.782
I'm the reason why everyone
here looks so good.

64
00:03:52.300 --> 00:03:54.506
My friend found this online.

65
00:03:54.507 --> 00:03:56.161
I don't know
what you're talking about.

66
00:03:56.162 --> 00:03:58.230
You lied to me. You said
it was for your portfolio...

67
00:03:58.231 --> 00:04:00.264
- Get ahold of yourself.
- Take this down!

68
00:04:00.265 --> 00:04:02.230
Hey. I am working right now.
okay? Hey! What are you...

69
00:04:02.231 --> 00:04:04.334
Don't touch her!

70
00:04:06.127 --> 00:04:07.920
Whoa. whoa. Riley.

71
00:04:07.921 --> 00:04:10.369
Let's get back to work.
Right now.

72
00:04:12.783 --> 00:04:14.299
Hey.

73
00:04:14.300 --> 00:04:16.783
I think it's time
to call it a night. okay?

74
00:04:18.472 --> 00:04:21.644
Frank. take care of this?

75
00:04:21.645 --> 00:04:23.679
Come on.
Let's get you out of here.

76
00:04:27.610 --> 00:04:31.403
Help! Help! Help!

77
00:04:57.783 --> 00:04:59.402
Stop. stop!

78
00:04:59.403 --> 00:05:02.162
Wait. wait. wait. stop! Stop!

79
00:05:48.403 --> 00:05:50.230
This is the new
east end hectare.

80
00:05:50.231 --> 00:05:52.885
We started emptying
the trucks into this section

81
00:05:52.886 --> 00:05:55.265
a couple weeks ago
after the old one got full up.

82
00:05:56.472 --> 00:05:58.264
I mean. if she'd been dumped
into the old site.

83
00:05:58.265 --> 00:05:59.609
we never would have seen her.

84
00:05:59.610 --> 00:06:01.609
- Lucky.
- Yeah.

85
00:06:01.610 --> 00:06:03.748
Was thinking I would buy
a lotto ticket on my way home.

86
00:06:05.334 --> 00:06:07.092
Yeah. you guys
got a system in place

87
00:06:07.093 --> 00:06:09.161
for tracking what part
of the city she comes from?

88
00:06:09.162 --> 00:06:10.885
Give me a sec.
I can narrow it down

89
00:06:10.886 --> 00:06:12.195
to within about four blocks.

90
00:06:12.196 --> 00:06:13.576
Thanks.

91
00:06:17.403 --> 00:06:20.817
What is she.
19. 20 years old tops?

92
00:06:21.955 --> 00:06:23.921
Bruising on the throat.

93
00:06:25.403 --> 00:06:28.196
Petechial hemorrhaging
in the eyes.

94
00:06:28.921 --> 00:06:30.714
She was strangled.

95
00:06:33.748 --> 00:06:36.885
New polish. but the nails
have been clipped and cleaned.

96
00:06:36.886 --> 00:06:38.782
Maybe she fought back

97
00:06:38.783 --> 00:06:41.471
and the killer rewarded her
with postmortem manicure.

98
00:06:41.472 --> 00:06:43.093
No trace evidence.

99
00:06:44.714 --> 00:06:47.506
These marks on her body.
they're not bruises.

100
00:06:47.507 --> 00:06:49.369
Stains maybe?

101
00:06:50.231 --> 00:06:52.195
These scrapes.
they didn't bleed.

102
00:06:52.196 --> 00:06:53.885
they were made postmortem.

103
00:06:53.886 --> 00:06:56.368
Maybe the killer dragged her
after she was killed.

104
00:06:56.369 --> 00:06:59.471
A person adjusts their grip
and repositions.

105
00:06:59.472 --> 00:07:01.989
These are deep and continuous.

106
00:07:01.990 --> 00:07:04.264
I'm not sure she was
dumped from that truck.

107
00:07:04.265 --> 00:07:07.576
I think she was dragged
here by a vehicle.

108
00:07:08.472 --> 00:07:10.402
Graff.

109
00:07:10.403 --> 00:07:12.954
Rear axle. another tarp.

110
00:07:12.955 --> 00:07:14.852
That loader
could have dragged her.

111
00:07:17.679 --> 00:07:20.989
Ainsley Scott.
Elmira. Ontario.

112
00:07:20.990 --> 00:07:23.817
She was to turn 19 next week.

113
00:07:25.300 --> 00:07:28.299
So if that isn't exactly
where she was dumped.

114
00:07:28.300 --> 00:07:30.609
does that mean we're looking
at more than just the east end?

115
00:07:30.610 --> 00:07:32.333
If she was dragged
from a different hectare.

116
00:07:32.334 --> 00:07:34.472
She could have been thrown
into any dumpster in the GTA.

117
00:07:42.334 --> 00:07:45.264
Mr. Scott. why did
Ainsley move to Toronto?

118
00:07:45.265 --> 00:07:48.057
Ainsley came to the city
to be famous.

119
00:07:50.403 --> 00:07:52.058
That's all she ever wanted.

120
00:07:55.024 --> 00:07:58.161
Uh. her mother
passed five years ago.

121
00:07:58.162 --> 00:07:59.575
a drunk driver.

122
00:07:59.576 --> 00:08:02.540
She had Ainsley in dance
and acting classes

123
00:08:02.541 --> 00:08:04.678
before her first holy communion.

124
00:08:04.679 --> 00:08:06.575
Lot of good that did her.

125
00:08:06.576 --> 00:08:08.885
"A lot of good that did her."

126
00:08:08.886 --> 00:08:12.299
referring to the sacrament
or the vocation?

127
00:08:12.300 --> 00:08:14.471
Take your pick.

128
00:08:14.472 --> 00:08:16.782
It's hard to shake
that Catholic guilt.

129
00:08:16.783 --> 00:08:18.471
No. I'm lapsed.

130
00:08:18.472 --> 00:08:20.471
Well. obviously.
something's bothering you. sir.

131
00:08:20.472 --> 00:08:22.126
You're evading eye contact.

132
00:08:22.127 --> 00:08:24.540
rubbing your neck
with one hand. nodding.

133
00:08:24.541 --> 00:08:27.126
That's the Holy Trinity
of non-verbal guilt right there.

134
00:08:27.127 --> 00:08:29.333
Are you insinuating that
I have something to do with

135
00:08:29.334 --> 00:08:31.264
my daughter's death?
- No. sir.

136
00:08:31.265 --> 00:08:33.610
I'm insinuating
that you think you did.

137
00:08:35.679 --> 00:08:38.644
Ainsley
called last week...

138
00:08:38.645 --> 00:08:40.230
...excited.

139
00:08:40.231 --> 00:08:42.161
"Daddy. I think
I got my big break."

140
00:08:42.162 --> 00:08:44.506
Said she needed
$700 for headshots.

141
00:08:44.507 --> 00:08:46.851
I told her I didn't have it.

142
00:08:46.852 --> 00:08:49.057
"Maybe your birthday.
sweetheart?"

143
00:08:49.058 --> 00:08:51.299
So she said
she'd find another way.

144
00:08:51.300 --> 00:08:52.920
Is this why
this happened to her.

145
00:08:52.921 --> 00:08:55.092
because she found another way?

146
00:08:57.472 --> 00:09:00.713
Um. did she tell you
what that. uh. big break was?

147
00:09:00.714 --> 00:09:03.023
I didn't wanna jinx it.

148
00:09:05.886 --> 00:09:07.369
Here.

149
00:09:08.576 --> 00:09:10.057
I'll give you a moment.

150
00:09:14.748 --> 00:09:16.471
If Ainsley's body
was dumped here.

151
00:09:16.472 --> 00:09:17.886
she was picked up on Friday.

152
00:09:28.093 --> 00:09:29.885
- Oh.
- Thank you.

153
00:09:29.886 --> 00:09:31.921
I got it. Here.
- Thank you.

154
00:09:41.024 --> 00:09:43.920
Sorry. detectives. She wasn't
dumped at her building.

155
00:09:43.921 --> 00:09:46.402
She's only been dead
three days tops.

156
00:09:46.403 --> 00:09:48.747
Well. there's no
collection on Sundays.

157
00:09:48.748 --> 00:09:51.782
so wherever she was dumped.
she was picked up on Monday.

158
00:09:51.783 --> 00:09:54.299
Judging by the way
her larynx was fractured.

159
00:09:54.300 --> 00:09:56.954
the killer most likely used
his elbow or forearm

160
00:09:56.955 --> 00:09:58.782
and put his entire
body weight on top of her

161
00:09:58.783 --> 00:10:00.195
to close her airway.

162
00:10:00.196 --> 00:10:02.195
Vaginal injuries. tearing.

163
00:10:02.196 --> 00:10:03.782
all consistent
with sexual assault.

164
00:10:03.783 --> 00:10:05.885
but an absence of seminal fluid.

165
00:10:05.886 --> 00:10:07.264
The killer wore a condom.
There's residue.

166
00:10:07.265 --> 00:10:09.126
But no DNA.

167
00:10:09.127 --> 00:10:12.057
Now we know that sexual
murders are committed

168
00:10:12.058 --> 00:10:15.230
by one of two kinds of people
with pathological disorders.

169
00:10:15.231 --> 00:10:17.782
Those who kill to hide
the sexual assault

170
00:10:17.783 --> 00:10:21.437
and those who find gratification
in the act of killing itself.

171
00:10:21.438 --> 00:10:24.747
The latter are planners.
Harder to catch.

172
00:10:24.748 --> 00:10:26.264
Explains the condom

173
00:10:26.265 --> 00:10:28.679
and the clipping and cleaning
of the fingernails.

174
00:10:29.610 --> 00:10:32.575
What about those. uh.
those blue marks on her skin?

175
00:10:32.576 --> 00:10:35.402
Results aren't back yet.
Most likely some sort of dye.

176
00:10:35.403 --> 00:10:37.540
Is this the trash from ident?

177
00:10:37.541 --> 00:10:38.920
Yeah.

178
00:10:38.921 --> 00:10:41.127
They appear to be
mostly fabric swatches.

179
00:10:45.990 --> 00:10:48.575
See the light pass through?

180
00:10:48.576 --> 00:10:50.713
There's pilling. It's cheap.

181
00:10:50.714 --> 00:10:52.333
Disperse blue.

182
00:10:52.334 --> 00:10:54.678
A derivative dye often used
in outdoor textiles.

183
00:10:54.679 --> 00:10:58.057
Exactly.
Outdoor blankets. tablecloths.

184
00:10:58.058 --> 00:11:01.299
When. uh. clothing manufacturers
use it to cut costs.

185
00:11:01.300 --> 00:11:04.851
given the right moisture
conditions. it can stain skin.

186
00:11:04.852 --> 00:11:07.299
Huh. Okay. so these swatches

187
00:11:07.300 --> 00:11:09.333
were caught up in the tarp
she was wrapped in.

188
00:11:09.334 --> 00:11:12.540
so what are we thinking?
Dumpster from a fabric store?

189
00:11:12.541 --> 00:11:14.989
Clothing manufacturer.
textile mill.

190
00:11:14.990 --> 00:11:18.092
somewhere that has its trash
collected on Mondays

191
00:11:18.093 --> 00:11:21.264
and no doubt
a. uh. CCTV dead zone.

192
00:11:24.265 --> 00:11:26.195
The killer.

193
00:11:26.196 --> 00:11:29.333
he keeps telling us
that he's smart.

194
00:11:29.334 --> 00:11:31.609
Let's believe him.

195
00:11:34.369 --> 00:11:36.230
Four down. two to go.

196
00:11:36.231 --> 00:11:38.816
There's no security cameras.
This could be it.

197
00:11:38.817 --> 00:11:41.023
Remote. not much traffic.

198
00:11:41.024 --> 00:11:42.851
Call in the ident team?

199
00:11:42.852 --> 00:11:46.057
Before we waste their time.
let's see if we're wasting ours.

200
00:12:01.231 --> 00:12:02.713
Bateman.

201
00:12:08.472 --> 00:12:10.195
Call them in.

202
00:12:10.196 --> 00:12:12.437
We found our dumpster.

203
00:12:12.438 --> 00:12:15.195
The owner of Walsh's
Textile Mill is in France.

204
00:12:15.196 --> 00:12:16.885
He's been there
for the last five months.

205
00:12:16.886 --> 00:12:19.230
Must be nice.
What about an employee?

206
00:12:19.231 --> 00:12:22.057
No. they didn't recognize
Ainsley from the photographs.

207
00:12:22.058 --> 00:12:23.782
They're mostly older women.
new Canadians.

208
00:12:23.783 --> 00:12:26.368
Probably don't wanna get on
the wrong side of the law.

209
00:12:26.369 --> 00:12:27.920
and it doesn't really fit
the profile. does it?

210
00:12:27.921 --> 00:12:30.540
No. our killer took his time.
He's entitled.

211
00:12:30.541 --> 00:12:32.126
Plus.
the land isn't fenced in.

212
00:12:32.127 --> 00:12:34.230
Anyone could have driven
in there and dumped the body.

213
00:12:34.231 --> 00:12:36.368
Anyone who knew there
weren't any security cameras.

214
00:12:36.369 --> 00:12:38.540
Which is why we're looking
into ex-employees

215
00:12:38.541 --> 00:12:40.713
and anyone in the neighborhood
on the sex offender registry.

216
00:12:40.714 --> 00:12:42.816
New visitor.

217
00:12:42.817 --> 00:12:45.195
Blood in the dumpster
from the textile mill

218
00:12:45.196 --> 00:12:46.851
is from our victim
in the landfill.

219
00:12:46.852 --> 00:12:48.954
But that's not
the only DNA I found.

220
00:12:48.955 --> 00:12:50.886
Ainsley might not be
the only victim.

221
00:12:53.990 --> 00:12:55.609
This is where your first
victim would've been

222
00:12:55.610 --> 00:12:56.989
before the load dragged her off.

223
00:12:56.990 --> 00:12:59.540
So. anything from
Walsh's Textile Mill

224
00:12:59.541 --> 00:13:01.195
would have been dumped here.

225
00:13:01.196 --> 00:13:03.126
Yeah. If it's from that
dumpster one month ago

226
00:13:03.127 --> 00:13:05.679
or one year ago.
then it's in this cell.

227
00:13:06.852 --> 00:13:09.402
You sure your dogs can smell
a body through all this trash?

228
00:13:09.403 --> 00:13:10.816
Up to 15 feet.

229
00:13:10.817 --> 00:13:12.299
30 in the water.

230
00:13:13.645 --> 00:13:14.817
Hmm.

231
00:13:25.507 --> 00:13:27.644
We got another one
deeper down!

232
00:13:27.645 --> 00:13:29.265
Most of one. anyway.

233
00:13:30.817 --> 00:13:32.747
This isn't just a crime scene.

234
00:13:32.748 --> 00:13:34.403
It's a graveyard.

235
00:13:43.369 --> 00:13:45.506
Victim number two.
Freya Klein. killed a month ago.

236
00:13:45.507 --> 00:13:47.023
still in possession
of a German driver's license.

237
00:13:47.024 --> 00:13:49.402
Freya was killed
in the same way Ainsley was.

238
00:13:49.403 --> 00:13:51.920
asphyxia with
a fractured larynx.

239
00:13:51.921 --> 00:13:54.299
There's no ID yet
on our Jane Doe.

240
00:13:54.300 --> 00:13:57.092
Her DNA was found in the textile
mill dumpster with the others

241
00:13:57.093 --> 00:13:58.782
and a broken hyoid bone

242
00:13:58.783 --> 00:14:00.299
indicates the same
cause of death.

243
00:14:00.300 --> 00:14:01.885
She must've been
in pretty bad shape

244
00:14:01.886 --> 00:14:04.230
if we needed a computer to
tell us what she looked like.

245
00:14:04.231 --> 00:14:06.506
Yeah. That still places her
body in the landfill

246
00:14:06.507 --> 00:14:07.782
for about a year.

247
00:14:07.783 --> 00:14:09.126
All three
were sexually assaulted.

248
00:14:09.127 --> 00:14:11.437
all three had
their fingernails clipped.

249
00:14:11.438 --> 00:14:13.713
Same MO. same killer.

250
00:14:13.714 --> 00:14:15.816
A year ago.
a month ago. and now.

251
00:14:15.817 --> 00:14:18.092
His offense cycle is speeding up
and we know that. uh.

252
00:14:18.093 --> 00:14:20.230
serial killers refine
their methods over time.

253
00:14:20.231 --> 00:14:22.575
but this guy. no mess. no DNA.

254
